# Sync and auth invariants

Non-negotiable for Phase 2 (see Phase 2 brief):

- Logged-out users keep the full local v1 experience.
- Local-only books never imply upload.
- Sync is async and must not block page/chapter navigation.
- Continuation is **explicit** — never silently replace this device's position.
- Each device keeps its own track; conflict policy is independent tracks, not LWW merge.
- Phase 2 syncs reading position/session metadata only — not annotations, not local book bytes.
- No credentials, tokens, or secrets in source, tests, docs, or the static client bundle.

## Ownership

- Reader/UI saves locally first; does not call the sync API ad hoc.
- `SyncCoordinator` owns queue, push/pull, cursor, retry/backoff.
- Auth failure must not erase local reading state.
- Push mutations must be idempotent; advance pull cursor only after successful local apply.

## Server (`server/`)

- Authorize every account-scoped resource.
- Seeded dev user (`testuser` / `testpass`) only when `SEED_TEST_USER=true` in compose.
- Keep API contracts aligned with client `AuthService` / sync transport interfaces.

## ❌ / ✅

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — open book jumps to remote position automatically
await reader.goTo(remoteSession.location);

// ✅ GOOD — offer continuation; preserve local track on dismiss
continuationStore.offer(remoteSession); // user picks Continue | Start from this device
```
